  "failure_category": "FM-1.1",
  "explanation": "The agent failed to correctly interpret the task specification regarding 'blocks' or 'layers' in the context of the 'Attention is All You Need' paper. It incorrectly summed the encoder and decoder layers, whereas the question implicitly refers to the encoder layers only for comparison with BERT's encoder layers.",
  "evidence": "The task asks 'How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?'. The agent correctly identified BERT base has 12 layers (encoder layers). However, for 'Attention is All You Need', it stated 'The architecture proposed in the \"Attention Is All You Need\" paper consists of 6 layers in both the encoder and decoder, totaling 12 layers.' and then calculated the difference as 12 - 12 = 0. This indicates a misinterpretation of 'encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need' as the total layers (encoder + decoder) instead of just the encoder layers (6)."
}
